WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:06.160
. David, I understand voting by mail, but
why should states accept ballots after Election

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.740
Day after all?

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.220
Election Day is Election Day.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.220
Fair question.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.749
Let's assume you're asking it in good faith.

00:00:13.749 --> 00:00:21.340
The of the population that wants to vote should
be allowed to vote up until Election Day.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:25.869
And if you want to vote absentee, you should
be allowed to do it.

00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:32.800
So the only possible correct solution is as
long as your ballot has been sent by Election

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:33.800
Day.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.840
It should count.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:41.200
And in particular, when you think so, before
I go further, if the ballot has to be received

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:46.240
by Election Day, as is the rule in some states
and I disagree with it, you really only have

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.770
until if you assume it could take four days
for the ballot to be delivered.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:53.750
You really only have until October 30th, the
thirty first to vote.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:55.590
But Election Day is November 3rd.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:01:01.940
Why should you be denied by four days when
you can send in your ballot?

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:07.130
If you are still able to do it before Election
Day, by Election Day, you should be allowed

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.130
to do it.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:14.340
Now, on top of that, when you recognize the
way in which the Postal Service has been attacked

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:19.680
by Donald Trump's postmaster general, he now
says that he's not doing any more stuff.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.680
Do we trust it?

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.680
Do we not?

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:27.119
There's just questions we don't want votes
to be able to be disqualified just because

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:29.810
the Postal Service delays the mail.

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:34.660
If the ballot is postmarked by November 3rd,
that is what should matter.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:40.759
Now, if you want to be really cynical, the
post office could as they gather the ballots

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:43.649
on November 2nd and November 3rd.

00:01:43.649 --> 00:01:48.430
Wait until November 4th and postmark them
then and get them disqualified that way.

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:54.890
We're now talking about a more sort of invasive
level of suppression.

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:59.600
But there is really no good reason for which
you should not have your vote counted as long

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.920
as you send it by Election Day.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:05.729
We have a pandemic expecting more vote by
mail than ever.

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:06.729
We're already seeing it.

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:10.680
We've already seen by some reports more than
60 million votes already cast.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.620
Could be close to half of the total electorate.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.660
It's unbelievable numbers.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:17.600
We want to make sure these votes are counted.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.050
And if you vote by November 3rd, it should
be counted.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:21.930
One last thought.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:25.050
Not only are we going to see more vote by
mail than ever before.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:31.830
We are going to see a lot of new voters voting
for the first time by mail.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.980
Some mistakes are going to be made.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:41.760
And I believe that we should as if we have
the goal not of being ticky tacky and figuring

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.800
out ways to disqualify ballots, which is what
Republicans want to do.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:51.560
What I want to do is we should do everything
we can to get as many people as possible legally

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:52.560
voting.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:59.940
We want time for people who make mistakes
on their ballots to be notified and to be

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:03.440
able to resubmit or decide to go in in person.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:06.990
And I know that that will sound weird to a
lot of people who want to be very, very litigious

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:11.650
and regimented and strict father morality
sort of approach.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:15.970
We believe that democracy is best served by
high voter participation.

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:20.220
And I do believe that then we should be doing
everything we can to get as many people to

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.080
successfully vote, period.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:27.460
And if you believe that, you, of course, should
be allowing every vote to be counted, that

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:28.220
is postmarked by Election Day.

